From b355d682e8dbb8009a6d37c402d27f67c396d8a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:34:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] grid: never size the block axis under a min- or max-content
 constraint

An auto-height grid container is laid out with an indefinite block size,
which taffy and its embedders (servo included) pass as
AvailableSpace::MaxContent. The track sizing algorithm read that as "sized
under a max-content constraint" and applied the constraint-only rules:
limited min-content contributions in place of minimum contributions, and
the max-content minimums step. Browsers never size the block axis under a
content constraint, so a `grid-template-rows: 0fr` row holding an
overflow:hidden (or min-height:0) item grew to the item's content height
where Chrome keeps it at 0, which broke the 0fr/1fr accordion pattern.

Restrict those rules to the inline axis, and treat a min-content block
size as indefinite as well, since a grid container's min-content block
size is just its laid-out block size (a 1fr row in a shrinking column
flexbox kept 0 instead of its content height). The new fixtures also cover
1fr rows and spanning auto rows in auto-height grids, which keep their
content-based sizes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
